{
  "title": "Rites on the Way to the Shrine of Imam Ali (a.s.) and Permission to Enter — Najaf",
  "data": "Before setting out, do ghusl, put on two clean garments and, if you can, some perfume (see [Etiquettes of Ziyarat](B3)). As you leave your house, say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ خَرَجْتُ مِنْ مَنْزِلِيْ اَبْغِيْ فَضْلَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE KHARAJTU MIN MANZILEE ABGHEE FADLAK\nO Allah, I leave my house seeking Your bounties\nوَاَزُوْرُ وَصِيَّ نَبِيِّكَ صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِمَا\nWA AZOORU WASIYYA NABIYYIKA SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHIMAA\nand to visit the successor of Your Prophet, Your blessings be upon them both.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَيَسِّرْ ذٰلِكَ لِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA FAYASSIR DHAALIKA LEE\nSo, O Allah, (please do) make it easy for me,\nوَسَبِّبِ الْمَزَارَ لَهٗ\nWA SABBIBIL MAZAARA LAH\nand pave the way for my visit to him,\nوَاخْلُفْنِيْ فِيْ عَاقِبَتِيْ وَحُزَانَتِيْ\nWAKHLUFNEE FEE A'AQIBATEE WA HUZAANATEE\nand take my place, while I am away, in my affairs and possessions\nبِاَحْسَنِ الْخِلَافَةِ\nBI-AHSANIL KHILAAFAH\nin the best way.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nThen set out, saying as you go:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHI WA SUBHAANALLAAHI WA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAH\nAll praise be to Allah, glory be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah.\nWhen you reach the trench of Kufa (near Masjid al-Hannanah, on the road from Kufa), stop and say:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ اَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBARU ALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Most Great. Allah is the Most Great.\nاَهْلَ الْكِبْرِيَاءِ وَالْمَجْدِ وَالْعَظَمَةِ\nAHLAL KIBRIYAA'I WAL MAJDI WAL A'ZAMAH\nO worthiest of exaltation, glorification, and grandeur.\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ اَهْلَ التَّكْبِيْرِ وَالتَّقْدِيْسِ\nALLAAHU AKBARU AHLAT TAKBEERI WAT TAQDEES\nAllah is the Most Great. O worthiest of being deemed Great, of sanctification,\nوَالتَّسْبِيْحِ وَالْاٰلَاءِ\nWAT TASBEEHI WAL AALAA'\nof glorification, and of granting bounties.\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ مِمَّا اَخَافُ وَاَحْذَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBARU MIMMAA AKHAAFU WA AHDHAR\nAllah is Greater than what I fear and what I worry about.\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ عِمَادِيْ وَعَلَيْهِ اَتَوَكَّلُ\nALLAAHU AKBARU I'MAADEE WA A'LAYHI ATAWAKKAL\nAllah is the Most Great; He is my support and on Him do I rely.\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ رَجَائِيْ وَاِلَيْهِ اُنِيْبُ\nALLAAHU AKBARU RAJAA'EE WA ILAYHI UNEEB\nAllah is the Most Great; He is my hope and to Him do I turn.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ وَلِيُّ نِعْمَتِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTA WALIYYU NI'MATEE\nO Allah, You are indeed the source of my blessings\nوَالْقَادِرُ عَلٰى طَلِبَتِيْ\nWAL QAADIRU A'LAA TALIBATEE\nand You are able to grant my request.\nتَعْلَمُ حَاجَتِيْ\nTA'LAMU HAAJATEE\nYou know my need\nوَمَا تُضْمِرُهٗ هَوَاجِسُ الصُّدُوْرِ\nWA MAA TUDMIRUHOO HAWAAJISUS SUDOOR\nand whatever is concealed by the premonitions of hearts\nوَخَوَاطِرُ النُّفُوْسِ\nWA KHAWAATIRUN NUFOOS\nand the thoughts of inner selves.\nفَاَسْاَلُكَ بِمُحَمَّدٍ الْمُصْطَفَى\nFA-AS'ALUKA BIMUHAMMADINIL MUSTAFAA\nI therefore beseech You in the name of Muhammad, the Chosen Prophet,\nالَّذِيْ قَطَعْتَ بِهٖ حُجَجَ الْمُحْتَجِّيْنَ\nALLADHEE QATA'TA BIHEE HUJAJAL MUHTAJJEEN\nthrough whom You have cut short the arguments of those who dispute\nوَعُذْرَ الْمُعْتَذِرِيْنَ\nWA U'DHRAL MU'TADHIREEN\nand the excuses of those who make excuses,\nوَجَعَلْتَهٗ رَحْمَةً لِلْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA JA'ALTAHOO RAHMATAN LIL A'ALAMEEN\nand whom You have decided to be mercy to the peoples,\nاَنْ لَا تَحْرِمَنِيْ ثَوَابَ زِيَارَةِ وَلِيِّكَ\nAN LAA TAHRIMANEE THAWAABA ZIYAARATI WALIYYIK\n(I beseech You) not to deprive me of the rewards of my visiting Your intimate servant,\nوَاَخِيْ نَبِيِّكَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَقَصْدَهٗ\nWA AKHEE NABIYYIKA AMEERIL MU'MINEENA WA QASDAH\nthe brother of Your Prophet, the Commander of the Faithful, and the reward of setting out to him,\nوَتَجْعَلَنِيْ مِنْ وَفْدِهِ الصَّالِحِيْنَ\nWA TAJ'ALANEE MIN WAFDIHIS SAALIHEEN\nand to include me with the virtuous delegation to him\nوَشِيْعَتِهِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ\nWA SHEE'ATIHIL MUTTAQEEN\nand with his pious adherents;\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\n(I beseech for that) in the name of Your mercy, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy.\nWhen the dome of the shrine comes into sight, say:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ عَلٰى مَا اخْتَصَّنِيْ بِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHI A'LAA MAKH TASSANEE BIH\nAll praise be to Allah, for He has conferred upon me exclusively\nمِنْ طِيْبِ الْمَوْلِدِ\nMIN TEEBIL MAWLID\nthe purity of my birth,\nوَاسْتَخْلَصَنِيْ اِكْرَامًا بِهٖ\nWASTAKHLASANEE IKRAAMAN BIH\nand has chosen me, honoring me thereby,\nمِنْ مُوَالَاةِ الْاَبْرَارِ\nMIN MUWAALAATIL ABRAAR\nfor loyalty to the pious,\nالسَّفَرَةِ الْاَطْهَارِ\nAS-SAFARATIL AT-HAAR\nthe pure envoys,\nوَالْخِيَرَةِ الْاَعْلَامِ\nWAL KHIYARATIL A'LAAM\nthe chosen ones and the guiding signs.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَتَقَبَّلْ سَعْيِيْ اِلَيْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA FATAQABBAL SA'YEE ILAYK\nO Allah, accept my striving toward You\nوَتَضَرُّعِيْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nWA TADARRU'EE BAYNA YADAYK\nand my earnest imploration in Your Presence\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِيْ لَا تَخْفٰى عَلَيْكَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE LAA TAKHFAA A'LAYK\nand (please do) forgive my sins that cannot be hidden from You.\nاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْغَفَّارُ\nINNAKA ANTALLAAHUL MALIKUL GHAFFAAR\nVerily, You are Allah, the King, the All-forgiving.\nAt the gate of Najaf, say:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ هَدَانَا لِهٰذَا\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE HADAANAA LIHAADHAA\nAll praise be to Allah Who has guided us to this;\nوَمَا كُنَّا لِنَهْتَدِيَ لَوْلَا اَنْ هَدَانَا اللّٰهُ\nWA MAA KUNNAA LINAHTADIYA LAWLAA AN HADAANALLAAH\nand we would not have found the way had it not been that Allah had guided us.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ سَيَّرَنِيْ فِيْ بِلَادِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE SAYYARANEE FEE BILAADIH\nAll praise be to Allah Who has made me travel through His lands,\nوَحَمَلَنِيْ عَلٰى دَوَابِّهٖ\nWA HAMALANEE A'LAA DAWAABBIH\nWho has caused me to ride His animals,\nوَطَوٰى لِيَ الْبَعِيْدَ\nWA TAWAA LIYAL BA'EED\nWho has made the distant space seem near for me,\nوَصَرَفَ عَنِّي الْمَحْذُوْرَ\nWA SARAFA A'NNIL MAHDHOOR\nWho has kept away from me what is dangerous,\nوَدَفَعَ عَنِّي الْمَكْرُوْهَ\nWA DAFA'A A'NNIL MAKROOH\nand Who has warded off from me what is hateful,\nحَتّٰى اَقْدَمَنِيْ حَرَمَ اَخِيْ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nHATTAA AQDAMANEE HARAMA AKHEE RASOOLIH\nuntil He brought me to the sanctuary of the brother of His Messenger,\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nmay Allah bless him and his Household.\nThen enter the town, saying:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ اَدْخَلَنِيْ هٰذِهِ الْبُقْعَةَ الْمُبَارَكَةَ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE ADKHALANEE HAADHIHIL BUQ'ATAL MUBAARAKAH\nAll praise be to Allah Who has allowed me to enter this blessed zone,\nالَّتِيْ بَارَكَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهَا\nALLATEE BAARAKALLAAHU FEEHAA\nwhich Allah has blessed\nوَاخْتَارَهَا لِوَصِيِّ نَبِيِّهٖ\nWAKHTAARAHAA LIWASIYYI NABIYYIH\nand has chosen for His Prophet’s Successor.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاجْعَلْهَا شَاهِدَةً لِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA FAJ'ALHAA SHAAHIDATAN LEE\nO Allah, (please do) make this zone witness for me.\nAt the first door of the shrine, say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بِبَابِكَ وَقَفْتُ\nALLAAHUMMA BIBAABIKA WAQAFT\nO Allah, I have stopped at Your door,\nوَبِفِنَائِكَ نَزَلْتُ\nWA BIFINAA'IKA NAZALT\nI have come to Your court,\nوَبِحَبْلِكَ اعْتَصَمْتُ\nWA BIHABLIKA' TASAMT\nto Your Cord do I cling,\nوَلِرَحْمَتِكَ تَعَرَّضْتُ\nWA LIRAHMATIKA TA'ARRADT\nYour mercy do I seek,\nوَبِوَلِيِّكَ صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِ تَوَسَّلْتُ\nWA BIWALIYYIKA SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHI TAWASSALT\nand through Your intimate servant, Your blessings be upon him, do I seek nearness to You.\nفَاجْعَلْهَا زِيَارَةً مَقْبُوْلَةً\nFAJ'ALHAA ZIYAARATAN MAQBOOLAH\nSo, (please do) make it an admissible visit\nوَدُعَاءً مُسْتَجَابًا\nWA DU'AA'AN MUSTAJAABAA\nand a responded supplication.\nAt the gate of the courtyard, say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذَا الْحَرَمَ حَرَمُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHAL HARAMA HARAMUK\nO Allah, this holy place is verily Yours,\nوَالْمَقَامَ مَقَامُكَ\nWAL MAQAAMA MAQAAMUK\nand this station is Your station,\nوَاَنَا اَدْخُلُ اِلَيْهِ اُنَاجِيْكَ\nWA ANAA ADKHULU ILAYHI UNAAJEEK\nand I am entering it to confide in You\nبِمَا اَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهٖ مِنِّيْ\nBIMAA ANTA A'LAMU BIHEE MINNEE\nabout what You know better than I do,\nوَمِنْ سِرِّيْ وَنَجْوَايَ\nWA MIN SIRREE WA NAJWAAY\nand better than my secrets and my whispered prayers.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الْحَنَّانِ الْمَنَّانِ الْمُتَطَوِّلِ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL HANNAANIL MANNAANIL MUTATAWWIL\nAll praise be to Allah, the All-benevolent, the All-favorer, the All-munificent,\nالَّذِيْ مِنْ تَطَوُّلِهٖ سَهَّلَ لِيْ زِيَارَةَ مَوْلَايَ بِاِحْسَانِهٖ\nALLADHEE MIN TATAWWULIHEE SAHHALA LEE ZIYAARATA MAWLAAYA BI-IHSAANIH\nWho, out of His munificence, has made it easy for me to visit my master,\nوَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِيْ عَنْ زِيَارَتِهٖ مَمْنُوْعًا\nWA LAM YAJ'ALNEE A'N ZIYAARATIHEE MAMNOO'AA\nWho has not made me banned from visiting him,\nوَلَا عَنْ وِلَايَتِهٖ مَدْفُوْعًا\nWA LAA A'N WILAAYATIHEE MADFOO'AA\nnor pushed me away from his (Divinely commissioned) guardianship;\nبَلْ تَطَوَّلَ وَمَنَحَ\nBAL TATAWWALA WA MANAH\nrather, He has been generous and bestowed (this favor).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ كَمَا مَنَنْتَ عَلَيَّ بِمَعْرِفَتِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA KAMAA MANANTA A'LAYYA BIMA'RIFATIH\nO Allah, just as You have conferred upon me with the favor of recognition of him,\nفَاجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ\nFAJ'ALNEE MIN SHEE'ATIH\nso also (please do) include me among his followers (Shi'ah)\nوَاَدْخِلْنِي الْجَنَّةَ بِشَفَاعَتِهٖ\nWA ADKHILNIL JANNATA BISHAFAA'ATIH\nand allow me to enter Paradise by means of his intercession,\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most merciful of all those who show mercy.\nThen go into the courtyard and say:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ اَكْرَمَنِيْ بِمَعْرِفَتِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE AKRAMANEE BIMA'RIFATIH\nAll praise be to Allah Who has honored me with the recognition of Him,\nوَمَعْرِفَةِ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nWA MA'RIFATI RASOOLIH\nthe recognition of His Messenger,\nوَمَنْ فَرَضَ عَلَيَّ طَاعَتَهٗ\nWA MAN FARADA A'LAYYA TAA'ATAH\nand the recognition of him the obedience to whom has been made incumbent upon me by Him\nرَحْمَةً مِنْهُ لِيْ\nRAHMATAN MINHU LEE\non account of His mercy to me,\nوَتَطَوُّلًا مِنْهُ عَلَيَّ\nWA TATAWWULAN MINHU A'LAYY\nHis favor that He bestowed upon me,\nوَمَنَّ عَلَيَّ بِالْاِيْمَانِ\nWA MANNA A'LAYYA BIL EEMAAN\nand His conferral upon me with faith.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ اَدْخَلَنِيْ حَرَمَ اَخِيْ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE ADKHALANEE HARAMA AKHEE RASOOLIH\nAll praise be to Allah Who has allowed me to enter the shrine of His Messenger’s brother\nوَاَرَانِيْهِ فِيْ عَافِيَةٍ\nWA ARAANEEHI FEE A'AFIYAH\nand has made me see this shrine while I enjoy good health.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ جَعَلَنِيْ مِنْ زُوَّارِ قَبْرِ وَصِيِّ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE JA'ALANEE MIN ZUWWAARI QABRI WASIYYI RASOOLIH\nAll praise be to Allah Who has included me with the visitors of the tomb of His Messenger’s successor.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAH\nI bear witness that there is no god but Allah,\nوَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nWAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nalone without having any associate,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nand I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\nجَاءَ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ\nJAA'A BIL HAQQI MIN I'NDILLAAH\nHe has conveyed the truth from Allah.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ عَلِيًّا عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ وَاَخُوْ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA A'LIYYAN A'BDULLAAHI WA AKHOO RASOOLILLAAH\nAnd I bear witness that Ali is the servant of Allah and the brother of Allah’s Messenger.\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ اللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ اللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBARULLAAHU AKBARULLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Most Great. Allah is the Most Great. Allah is the Most Great.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WALLAAHU AKBAR\nThere is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Most Great.\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ عَلٰى هِدَايَتِهٖ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI A'LAA HIDAAYATIH\nAll praise be to Allah for His guidance\nوَتَوْفِيْقِهٖ لِمَا دَعَا اِلَيْهِ مِنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ\nWA TAWFEEQIHEE LIMAA DA'AA ILAYHI MIN SABEELIH\nand for granting me success in what He has called to of His path.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ اَفْضَلُ مَقْصُوْدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA AFDALU MAQSOOD\nO Allah, You are verily the most excellent besought One\nوَاَكْرَمُ مَاْتِيٍّ\nWA AKRAMU MA'TIYY\nand the most generous of all to whom one comes.\nوَقَدْ اَتَيْتُكَ مُتَقَرِّبًا اِلَيْكَ\nWA QAD ATAYTUKA MUTAQARRIBAN ILAYK\nI thus have come to You, seeking nearness to You\nبِنَبِيِّكَ نَبِيِّ الرَّحْمَةِ\nBINABIYYIKA NABIYYIR RAHMAH\nin the name of Your Prophet, the Prophet of Mercy\nوَبِاَخِيْهِ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nWA BI-AKHEEHI AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\nand in the name of his brother, the Commander of the Faithful,\nعَلِيِّ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ عَلَيْهِمَا السَّلَامُ\nA'LIYYIBNI ABEE TAALIBIN A'LAYHIMAS SALAAM\nAli the son of Abu Talib, peace be upon them both.\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nSo, (please do) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَلَا تُخَيِّبْ سَعْيِيْ\nWA LAA TUKHAYYIB SA'YEE\ndo not disappoint my efforts,\nوَانْظُرْ اِلَيَّ نَظْرَةً رَحِيْمَةً تَنْعَشُنِيْ بِهَا\nWANZUR ILAYYA NAZRATAN RAHEEMATAN TAN'ASHUNEE BIHAA\n(please) grant me a merciful look from You through which You refresh me,\nوَاجْعَلْنِيْ عِنْدَكَ وَجِيْهًا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nWAJ'ALNEE I'NDAKA WAJEEHAN FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nmake me illustrious in Your view in this world as well as the world to come,\nوَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ\nWA MINAL MUQARRABEEN\nand make me of those brought near to You.\nWalk on to the door of the portico, stop there and say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon Allah’s Messenger\nاَمِيْنِ اللّٰهِ عَلٰى وَحْيِهٖ وَعَزَائِمِ اَمْرِهِ\nAMEENILLAAHI A'LAA WAHYIHEE WA A'ZAA'IMI AMRIH\nwhom Allah has entrusted with His Revelations and with His determined commandments,\nالْخَاتِمِ لِمَا سَبَقَ\nAL-KHAATIMI LIMAA SABAQ\nwho sealed the previous Messages,\nوَالْفَاتِحِ لِمَا اسْتُقْبِلَ\nWAL FAATIHI LIMAS TUQBIL\npaved the way to the coming blessings,\nوَالْمُهَيْمِنِ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ كُلِّهٖ\nWAL MUHAYMINI A'LAA DHAALIKA KULLIH\nand who prevails over all that.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nMay the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon him, too.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى صَاحِبِ السَّكِيْنَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA SAAHIBIS SAKEENAH\nPeace be upon the holder of tranquility.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَدْفُوْنِ بِالْمَدِيْنَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL MADFOONI BIL MADEENAH\nPeace be upon the one buried at al-Madinah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَنْصُوْرِ الْمُؤَيَّدِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL MANSOORIL MU'AYYAD\nPeace be upon the one granted victory and support (by Allah).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَبِي الْقَاسِمِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA ABIL QAASIMI MUHAMMADIBNI A'BDILLAAH\nPeace be upon Abu’l-Qasim, Muhammad the son of `Abdullah.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nMay the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon him, too.\nThen enter the portico, right foot first, and at the door of the shrine ask permission to enter:\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAH\nI bear witness that there is no god but Allah,\nوَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nWAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nalone without having any associate,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nand I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\nجَاءَ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ عِنْدِهٖ وَصَدَّقَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nJAA'A BIL HAQQI MIN I'NDIHEE WA SADDAQAL MURSALEEN\nHe has conveyed the truth from Him and verified the (past) Messengers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA RASOOLALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah!\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَبِيْبَ اللّٰهِ وَخِيَرَتَهٗ مِنْ خَلْقِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HABEEBALLAAHI WA KHIYARATAHOO MIN KHALQIH\nPeace be upon you, O most-beloved of Allah and best of His beings!\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon the Commander of the Faithful:\nعَبْدِ اللّٰهِ وَاَخِيْ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nA'BDILLAAHI WA AKHEE RASOOLILLAAH\nthe servant of Allah and the brother of Allah’s Messenger.\nيَا مَوْلَايَ يَا اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nYAA MAWLAAYA YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEEN\nO master, O Commander of the Faithful!\nعَبْدُكَ وَابْنُ عَبْدِكَ وَابْنُ اَمَتِكَ\nA'BDUKA WABNU A'BDIKA WABNU AMATIK\nI, your slave and the son of your slave and your bondmaid,\nجَاءَكَ مُسْتَجِيْرًا بِذِمَّتِكَ\nJAA'AKA MUSTAJEERAN BIDHIMMATIK\nhave come to you seeking the refuge of your protection,\nقَاصِدًا اِلٰى حَرَمِكَ\nQAASIDAN ILAA HARAMIK\ndirecting to your shrine,\nمُتَوَجِّهًا اِلٰى مَقَامِكَ\nMUTAWAJJIHAN ILAA MAQAAMIK\nturning my face toward your place,\nمُتَوَسِّلًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَعَالٰى بِكَ\nMUTAWASSILAN ILALLAAHI TA'AALAA BIK\nand begging Almighty Allah in your name.\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا مَوْلَايَ\nA'ADKHULU YAA MAWLAAY\nMay I enter, O master?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nA'ADKHULU YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEEN\nMay I enter, O Commander of the Faithful?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ\nA'ADKHULU YAA HUJJATALLAAH\nMay I enter, O argument of Allah?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا اَمِيْنَ اللّٰهِ\nA'ADKHULU YAA AMEENALLAAH\nMay I enter, O trustee of Allah?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا مَلَائِكَةَ اللّٰهِ الْمُقِيْمِيْنَ فِيْ هٰذَا الْمَشْهَدِ\nA'ADKHULU YAA MALAA'IKATALLAAHIL MUQEEMEENA FEE HAADHAL MASH-HAD\nMay I enter, O angels of Allah who reside in this shrine?\nيَا مَوْلَايَ اَتَاْذَنُ لِيْ بِالدُّخُوْلِ\nYAA MAWLAAYA ATA'DHANU LEE BID DUKHOOL\nO master, may you permit me to enter\nاَفْضَلَ مَا اَذِنْتَ لِاَحَدٍ مِنْ اَوْلِيَائِكَ\nAFDALA MAA ADHINTA LI-AHADIN MIN AWLIYAA'IK\nin the best way of permission you have ever given to any of your devotees?\nفَاِنْ لَمْ اَكُنْ لَهٗ اَهْلًا فَاَنْتَ اَهْلٌ لِذٰلِكَ\nFA-IN LAM AKUN LAHOO AHLAN FA-ANTA AHLUN LIDHAALIK\nIf I am not worthy of it, you are worthy of granting it.\nThen kiss the threshold and, stepping in with your right foot, say as you enter:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAH\nIn the Name of Allah (I begin), in Allah (I trust),\nوَفِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nWA FEE SABEELILLAAH\non the way of Allah,\nوَعَلٰى مِلَّةِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nWA A'LAA MILLATI RASOOLILLAAH\nand on the norm of the Messenger of Allah (I proceed),\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nmay Allah bless him and his Household.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيْ وَارْحَمْنِيْ وَتُبْ عَلَيَّ\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEE WARHAMNEE WA TUB A'LAYY\nO Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me and accept my repentance,\nاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nINNAKA ANTAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM\nfor You are the Oft-Returning, the Most Merciful.\nThen walk on until you face the tomb, and recite the [First Ziyarat](AK5) there.",
  "merits": "These are the rites that open the first general ziyarat of Imam Ali (a.s.), as Shaykh al-Mufid, al-Shahid, Sayyid Ibn Tawus and others have recorded them, and as Shaykh Abbas al-Qummi gives them in Mafatih al-Jinan: from leaving home, through the approach to Najaf and the shrine, to asking permission at the door of the dome. The ziyarat itself, recited at the tomb, is the [First Ziyarat](AK5).\n\nAt the sight of the dome, al-Qummi adds that when longing and joy overcome the pilgrim and he wishes to turn wholly to the Imam, he may praise him in whatever words he can, and he quotes some verses of Shaykh al-Uzri's qasida for this. He asks the pilgrim to convey his greetings at the shrine and to remember him in prayer.\n\nThrough an authentic chain of authority, Shaykh al-Tusi has reported on the authority of Muhammad ibn Muslim that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said, \"Almighty Allah has not created a category of creatures bigger in number than angels. Verily, seventy thousand angels descend every day to circumambulate the Much-Frequented House. Then, they circumambulate the Holy Ka'bah. Then, they visit the tomb of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) to greet him. Then, they visit the tomb of Imam Ali Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) to greet him. Then, they visit the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) to greet him. They then ascend back to the skies. Verily, if one visits Amir al-Mu'minin with full recognition of his right, being neither arrogant nor conceited, Almighty Allah shall decide for him the reward of one hundred thousand martyrs, forgive his past and coming sins, raise him among the secure, and make easy for him the calling to account; and he will be received by the angels. As he returns home, these angels will visit him when he is ill. When he dies, these angels will follow him to his grave, imploring Almighty Allah's forgiveness for him.\"\n\nIn Farhat al-Ghari, Sayyid Abd al-Karim ibn Tawus reports that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said, \"As for one who visits the tomb of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) walking, Almighty Allah shall verily decide for him the reward of one hajj and one 'umrah. If he returns walking, Almighty Allah shall decide for him the reward of two hajjs and two 'umrahs.\"\n\nImam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is also reported to have said to Ibn Marid, \"As for anyone who visits the tomb of my grandfather with recognition of his right, Almighty Allah shall decide for him the reward of an accepted hajj and an admissible 'umrah. Ibn Marid, I swear by Allah that He shall never give to Hellfire a foot that was dusted in the course of visiting Amir al-Mu'minin, walking or riding. Ibn Marid, write down this saying in gold.\"\n\nAccording to the narrations, Almighty Allah has made the tombs of Imam Ali (a.s.) and his immaculate descendants shelters for the fearful, refuges for the distressed, and places of safety for the people of the earth: any aggrieved person who visits them, Allah relieves him; any sick person, Allah heals him; and whoever seeks safety there, Allah grants it to him."
}
